{"id": "EUVD-2022-56069", "enisaUuid": "c8b2c61d-4b42-37f3-a762-50233bc27ab6", "description": "Penta Security WAPPLES 4.0.54.1, 5.0, and 6.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows authenticated attackers to download arbitrary files via the name parameter of /webapi/file/transfer. Attackers can send GET requests with type=db_backup and ../ sequences in name to read files like /etc/passwd, and a hardcoded systemi account makes authentication effectively trivial. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-19.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:35", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://medium.com/@_sadshade/wapples-web-application-firewall-multiple-vulnerabilities-35bdee52c8fb", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/other/wapples-firewall-lfi.yaml", "https://www.pentasecurity.com/product/wapples/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/penta-security-wapples-4.0.54.1-5.0-6.0-path-traversal-via-webapi-file-transfer"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5wwc-x9f3-f86v", "CVE-2022-51025"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7668e281-d8fc-316e-9abd-ccc1a28cf0d7", "product": {"name": "WAPPLES", "vendor": {"name": "Penta Security Systems"}}, "product_version": "5.0"}, {"id": "ac7db1c9-5c70-3140-a5fe-6284ead864cb", "product": {"name": "WAPPLES", "vendor": {"name": "Penta Security Systems"}}, "product_version": "4.0.54.1"}, {"id": "c21f0dba-5b38-3630-b887-2ec62748d039", "product": {"name": "WAPPLES", "vendor": {"name": "Penta Security Systems"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "56965188-98da-3b37-a61b-10513bf10ba3", "vendor": {"name": "Penta Security Systems"}}], "isExploited": false}